{"content":[{"c":["BANISH, BANISHMENT"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Exclusion of a person from a country or group as a form of punishment."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["“Banishment” or a similar word is used in the Bible to describe God’s judgment on Adam and Eve (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.3.23-24","r":"Gen.3.23-24","rawR":"Gen.3.23-24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.3.23-24","value":"Gen.3.23-24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 3:23-24"},") and on Cain (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.4.9-14","r":"Gen.4.9-14","rawR":"Gen.4.9-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.4.9-14","value":"Gen.4.9-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:9-14"},"), Absalom’s exile from his father David (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.13.37-39","r":"2Sam.13.37-39","rawR":"2Sam.13.37-39","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.13.37-39","value":"2Sam.13.37-39"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 13:37-39"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.14.13-14","r":"2Sam.14.13-14","rawR":"2Sam.14.13-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.14.13-14","value":"2Sam.14.13-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"14:13-14"},"), and Israel’s exile from the Promised Land (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.30.1","r":"Deut.30.1","rawR":"Deut.30.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.30.1","value":"Deut.30.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 30:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.11.12","r":"Isa.11.12","rawR":"Isa.11.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.11.12","value":"Isa.11.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Is 11:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.16.15","r":"Jer.16.15","rawR":"Jer.16.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.16.15","value":"Jer.16.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 16:15"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.4.13","r":"Ezek.4.13","rawR":"Ezek.4.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.4.13","value":"Ezek.4.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 4:13"},"). During the exile, it was included in a list of punishments for those who disobeyed God or the Persian king Artaxerxes (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.26","r":"Ezra.7.26","rawR":"Ezra.7.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.26","value":"Ezra.7.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:26"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":["The Mosaic law specified that an Israelite should be “cut off” from the people of God for various offenses, such as failure to circumcise a male child (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.17.12,14","r":"Gen.17.12,14","rawR":"Gen.17.12,14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.17.12,14","value":"Gen.17.12,14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 17:12, 14"},"), eating leavened bread during Passover (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.12.15","r":"Exod.12.15","rawR":"Exod.12.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.12.15","value":"Exod.12.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ex 12:15"},"), making an unholy animal sacrifice (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.17.1-4","r":"Lev.17.1-4","rawR":"Lev.17.1-4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.17.1-4","value":"Lev.17.1-4"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 17:1-4"},"), eating blood (v ",{"href":"?bref=Lev.17.10","r":"Lev.17.10","rawR":"Lev.17.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.17.10","value":"Lev.17.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"10"},"), sinning deliberately (",{"href":"?bref=Num.15.30-31","r":"Num.15.30-31","rawR":"Num.15.30-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.15.30-31","value":"Num.15.30-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 15:30-31"},"), or failing to undergo ceremonial cleansing after contact with a dead body (",{"href":"?bref=Num.19.11-20","r":"Num.19.11-20","rawR":"Num.19.11-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.19.11-20","value":"Num.19.11-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"19:11-20"},"). The term “cut off” probably meant exclusion from the social and religious life of the community (cf. ",{"href":"?bref=John.9.18-23,34","r":"John.9.18-23,34","rawR":"John.9.18-23,34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"John.9.18-23,34","value":"John.9.18-23,34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jn 9:18-23, 34"},"). After the exile, when the whole nation of Israel had been “banished,” disinheritance and permanent excommunication from God’s people were made official punishments (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.10.7-8","r":"Ezra.10.7-8","rawR":"Ezra.10.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.10.7-8","value":"Ezra.10.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 10:7-8"},"). The Romans, like other conquerors before them, practiced deportation in various forms. Controversy among the Jews led to the banishment of Jews from Rome under Emperor Claudius (",{"href":"?bref=Acts.18.2","r":"Acts.18.2","rawR":"Acts.18.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Acts.18.2","value":"Acts.18.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Acts 18:2"},"). The author of Revelation was banished to the island of Patmos during Roman persecution (",{"href":"?bref=Rev.1.9","r":"Rev.1.9","rawR":"Rev.1.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Rev.1.9","value":"Rev.1.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Rv 1:9"},"). More severe forms of banishment included permanent exclusion from an area, loss of citizenship, and confiscation of all goods and property."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=DiasporaoftheJews_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"DiasporaoftheJews_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"DiasporaoftheJews_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Diaspora of the Jews"},"."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BanishBanishment","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 3:23-24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.3.23-24","rawQueryValue":"Gen.3.23-24","sourceRefExact":"Gen.3.23-24"},{"anchorText":"4:9-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.4.9-14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.4.9-14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.4.9-14"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 13:37-39","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.13.37-39","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.13.37-39","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.13.37-39"},{"anchorText":"14:13-14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.14.13-14","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.14.13-14","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.14.13-14"},{"anchorText":"Dt 30:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.30.1","rawQueryValue":"Deut.30.1","sourceRefExact":"Deut.30.1"},{"anchorText":"Is 11:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.11.12","rawQueryValue":"Isa.11.12","sourceRefExact":"Isa.11.12"},{"anchorText":"Jer 16:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.16.15","rawQueryValue":"Jer.16.15","sourceRefExact":"Jer.16.15"},{"anchorText":"Ez 4:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.4.13","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.4.13","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.4.13"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 7:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.7.26","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.7.26","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.7.26"},{"anchorText":"Gn 17:12, 14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.17.12,14","rawQueryValue":"Gen.17.12,14","sourceRefExact":"Gen.17.12,14"},{"anchorText":"Ex 12:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Exod.12.15","rawQueryValue":"Exod.12.15","sourceRefExact":"Exod.12.15"},{"anchorText":"Lv 17:1-4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.17.1-4","rawQueryValue":"Lev.17.1-4","sourceRefExact":"Lev.17.1-4"},{"anchorText":"10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.17.10","rawQueryValue":"Lev.17.10","sourceRefExact":"Lev.17.10"},{"anchorText":"Nm 15:30-31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.15.30-31","rawQueryValue":"Num.15.30-31","sourceRefExact":"Num.15.30-31"},{"anchorText":"19:11-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.19.11-20","rawQueryValue":"Num.19.11-20","sourceRefExact":"Num.19.11-20"},{"anchorText":"Jn 9:18-23, 34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=John.9.18-23,34","rawQueryValue":"John.9.18-23,34","sourceRefExact":"John.9.18-23,34"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 10:7-8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.10.7-8","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.10.7-8","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.10.7-8"},{"anchorText":"Acts 18:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Acts.18.2","rawQueryValue":"Acts.18.2","sourceRefExact":"Acts.18.2"},{"anchorText":"Rv 1:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Rev.1.9","rawQueryValue":"Rev.1.9","sourceRefExact":"Rev.1.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"9bbb5cc1386d664e931b197c472627a2011a634cc418eace7f992b11edddc9e1","sourceItemName":"BanishBanishment","sourceItemOrder":64,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BanishBanishment","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Banish, Banishment","title":"Banish, Banishment","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}